# PROJECT PLANNING 

## Purpose

The purpose of this Project Planning document is to define how the Emergency Department Patient Flow Transformation project will be delivered.
This plan outlines the project activities, delivery approach, timeline, resources, milestones, dependencies, and management approach required to successfully implement the transformation programme.


# PROJECT DELIVERY APPROACH 

The project will follow a structured hybrid delivery approach combining:

## PRINCE2 Principles

Used for:
- Governance
- Business justification
- Risk management
- Stage approvals
- Project control

## Agile Delivery Practices

Used for:
- User feedback
- Solution improvement
- Testing
- Iterative development

This approach allows strong governance while ensuring healthcare users are involved throughout delivery.


# WORK BREAKDOWN STRUCTURE  (WBS)

The project will be divided into five major delivery phases.



# Phase 1: PROJECT INITIATION 

Duration: Month 1 - Month 2

Activities:
- Confirm project objectives
- Approve business case
- Establish project governance
- Identify stakeholders
- Define project requirements
- Create communication approach

Deliverables:
- Project Charter
- Governance Structure
- Stakeholder Management Plan
- Initial Project Plan


# Phase 2: ANALYSIS AND SOLUTION DESIGN 

Duration: Month 3 - Month 5

Activities:
- Analyse current processes
- Gather user requirements
- Review existing systems
- Define solution requirements
- Complete security assessment
- Design future patient flow process

Deliverables:
- Requirements Document
- Future State Process Map
- Solution Design
- Data Protection Assessment


# Phase 3: DEVELOPMENT AND IMPLEMENTATION PREPARATION 

Duration: Month 6 - Month 8

Activities:
- Configure digital solution
- Complete system integration
- Develop training materials
- Perform technical testing
- Prepare implementation plan

Deliverables:
- Configured Solution
- Testing Plan
- Training Materials
- Implementation Readiness Report


# Phase 4: IMPLEMENTATION AND DEPLOYMENT 

Duration: Month 9 - Month 11

Activities:
- Pilot implementation
- User acceptance testing
- Staff training
- System rollout
- Monitor performance
- Manage issues

Deliverables:
- Live Solution
- Trained Users
- Implementation Report
- Performance Monitoring Dashboard


# Phase 5: CLOSURE AND HANDOVER
Duration: 12 Months

Activities:
- Review project outcomes
- Complete handover
- Measure initial benefits
- Capture lessons learned
- Close project

Deliverables:
- Project Closure Report
- Lessons Learned Document
- Operational Handover Pack
- Benefits Realisation Plan

# PROJECT MILESTONES

## Milestone 1

Project Approval Completed
-Target: End of Month 1
-Success Criteria: Business Case approved and project authorised.


## Milestone 2

Requirements Completed
-Target: End of Month 3
-Success Criteria: Clinical and technical requirements agreed.

## Milestone 3

Solution Design Approved
-Target: End of Month 5
-Success Criteria: Future solution approved by stakeholders.

## Milestone 4

Testing Completed
-Target: End of Month 8
-Success Criteria: Solution successfully tested.

 
## Milestone 5

Go-Live Completed
-Target: End of Month 11
-Success Criteria: Solution implemented and users trained.


## Milestone 6

Project Closure
-Target: End of Month 12
-Success Criteria: Project transitioned into business-as-usual operations.


